myos in the libc crate (0.2.189, the one the pinned nightly's std is
built on): the mlibc flavour of the myos targets, `target_os = "myos"`
with `target_env = "mlibc"`, a unix target of the `linux_like` family
(mlibc's Linux ABI headers), with the signal numbers, sa_flags and
layouts where myos's headers differ
(toolchain/mlibc/sysdeps/myos/include/abi-bits). Applied by wire-myos.py
to the copy std's workspace vendors. toolchain/std/abi-check.sh compares
it with the C headers.

Adapted from Managarm's port of the crate, another system on mlibc
(patches 0001-Add-managarm-support.patch and
0003-managarm-Add-miscellaneous-bindings.patch of
https://github.com/managarm/bootstrap-managarm, patches/rust-libc; by
no92, Alexander van der Grinten and the Managarm contributors). A patch
to the libc crate: MIT OR Apache-2.0, as the crate
(THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

